                .and_then(CssGenericComponentValueList::cast)
                .is_some()
            {
                CommentPlacement::Default(comment)
            } else {
                CommentPlacement::leading(preceding_node.clone(), comment)
            }
        }
        _ => CommentPlacement::Default(comment),
    }
}
```

## Functions handling name/colon/value boundaries

There are two boundary-check helpers plus their callers. For SCSS variables:

- `handle_scss_variable_declaration_comment` places comments as dangling on the variable declaration for both the `$color/* c */:` (name–colon) and `:`–value cases.
- `is_between_variable_colon_and_value` returns true when the comment starts at or after the colon's trimmed range end and before the value's first token start.

For generic properties:

- `handle_generic_property_comment` handles the colon–value case as trailing, the name–colon case as dangling, and a name-followed-by-value-list case as trailing.
- `is_between_property_colon_and_value` uses the same colon-end/value-start comparison logic. Its inline note says `a { color: /* comment */ red; }` "belongs to the colon/value boundary."

The `is_between_property_colon_and_value` core check:

```rust
comment_start >= colon.text_trimmed_range().end() && comment_start < value_start
```

(The variable version `is_between_variable_colon_and_value` uses the identical comparison.)

## `place_comment` match arms

`place_comment` chains handlers with `or_else` rather than using a `match`:

```rust
handle_scss_map_trailing_separator_comment(comment)
    .or_else(place_separated_list_comment)
    .or_else(handle_scss_list_trailing_separator_comment)
    .or_else(handle_scss_each_value_list_comment)
    .or_else(handle_scss_expression_item_trailing_line_comment)
    .or_else(handle_scss_at_root_selector_comment)
    .or_else(handle_scss_else_clause_comment)
    .or_else(handle_function_comment)
    .or_else(handle_media_separator_comment)
    // Handle SCSS variable name/colon comments before generic properties.
    .or_else(handle_scss_variable_declaration_comment)
    .or_else(handle_generic_property_comment)
    .or_else(handle_declaration_name_comment)
    .or_else(handle_complex_selector_comment)
    .or_else(handle_global_suppression)
```

Note the ordering comment: `handle_scss_variable_declaration_comment` is placed before `handle_generic_property_comment` to handle SCSS variable name/colon comments first.

